+Text output is a table with one row per session: agent (`harness:model#effort`, from the bound dispatches' routes, else the session's own event models and the models subjects declare for it, else the model its recording says served it, effort unnamed when it served several; the harness alone when none establishes one; a coordinate that carries the row's harness as a prefix names it once; one whose prefix names another harness establishes none and is shown beside the agent, `claude (route codex:gpt-6.1-sol#high)`), roles (impl, review, orch, integ), the shortest unique session id prefix of at least eight characters, runs, spans, the disjoint token total, the money columns, and a status (`complete`, `subtotal`, `split ×N`, `shared ×N`, `live`, `unmeasured` or `withheld`); a list price in doubt shows as `least–most`. With a price table the money columns are the list-price estimate, then the harness-written estimate; without one the harness-written estimate alone, and a footer line says how to install a table. The `total` row is the union figure with its status, with a row per accounting partition when it spans several, the `total with estimates` row when a participant's estimate touches it, and with `--allocate` the allocated total beside it; `unattributed shared` holds everything of each session outside it, its unattributed part and its shares of unselected items (`unselected item`), with a line naming each session's reasons; one line counts the qualifications `--detail` explains; a `children` line per parent of native children names its bound rows, the children bound to unselected work, and the unassigned figure outside the total, and a `family` line its reconciliation and each residual counter that does not reconcile. `--detail` prints the per-category report instead. `--by` groups counted rows with one subtotal per group, never adding incompatible accounting domains. `--json` adds the table's rows, total, allocated total, unattributed figure, qualification count, groups, families and price table under `table`, each session's segments, shares, run figures and unattributed parts under `sessions[].split`, allocated figures under `work[].allocated`, the price table under `prices`, and the footprint under `footprint`.
+
+With `--commit <rev>` the target is a commit. Git resolves the revision, and the commit maps to the change that records it: a patchset head or the integrated commit decides first, and otherwise a commit inside a change's current patchset range belongs to that change. The view embeds the change's `arc-cost/1` document unchanged and adds the commit, its position ("2 of 3 commits") and its sibling commits, and states that the change's figures are shared by those commits and that none is per commit. Each role trailer on the commit lists the sessions recorded for that role. `Implemented-by` lists the sessions bound as implementer to the change's runs whose route model, effort and a prefix naming the executor's harness dropped, equals the trailer's model. `Reviewed-by` lists the sessions bound as reviewer on the same terms and the sessions, bound or not, whose events give them the reviewer role, and `Planned-by` and `Orchestrated-by` those whose events give them the orchestrator role, whose own model equals the trailer's: the models its own events, or a subject recorded on its behalf, declared in the role, else the one model its recording says served it (`model_source`), never the invoker's model on an event recorded on its behalf. A session in the role of the trailer's harness with no such model is listed unmatched (`unestablished`). A matching session's figure is its whole figure, shared exactly as the change view shares it, with the change's share beside it when the view divides the session, and its `status` is the word the change's table gives its row, beside its `measurement` status. A trailer no recorded session answers and no session is unmatched for reads `no session recorded`, never zero. A commit no change records answers `no change records this commit`, shows no figure, and succeeds. The lookup follows the aggregate read rule: each change whose state cannot be read is named with its error on stderr and the command succeeds. A lookup that skipped one never answers that no-match: it answers `no readable change records this commit` naming them, with `lookup.status` `unresolved`; a match found beside one is shown with `lookup.status` `may-not-be-unique` and a line saying so; `lookup.unreadable` lists them, and a lookup that read every change carries no `lookup`. A commit that several changes record is refused, naming them. With `--commit`, `--json` emits `arc-cost-commit/1`, which wraps the embedded `arc-cost/1`.
