+===== arc cost evidence --help =====
+Write the evidence `cost show` divides its sessions by to standard output, as a `tapes-attribution-evidence/1` file tapes reads, or into a directory of such files
+
+The selection is `cost show`'s: change ids and journal artifacts, `--tag`, `--footprint`, `--since`/`--until` and `--all`, read the same way. Export `--all` for exact figures: a participant's division rests on every piece of work it took part in, not only the selected one. The first line is the header, whose producer is `arc/<version>`. A session `cost show` gives a figure writes the evidence that decides it, every record at tier `bound`. An executor the ledger gives one run writes one `binding` with no span, which tapes reads as the whole session; one with several runs writes a `binding` per run, its span from the dispatch to the recorded `run end`, or to `written_at` while the run has none, with the run's role. A participant divided by its own events writes one `event` per event, with the role its kind gives it; one acting on a single piece of work writes a `binding` with no span, with its role when it has one. A participant the ledger does not divide, because an item only an event recorded on its behalf names, or a ledger record that could not be read, writes nothing and is counted. A session `cost show` names without a figure writes nothing and is counted. Each record's work is the change id or journal artifact as `cost show` names it, as `label`; `commits` holds the commits the change made itself (full object names), and is left out for a change that has none and for a journal artifact; `repository` is the repository's `origin` remote URL without its user information, query or fragment, and is left out when there is none or it names a place on this machine. A change's commits are those `cost note` finds for it less the current-patchset commits of every change below it in a stack, and always include its own integration commit. A change is below another when it is open or integrated and its current patchset head, different from the other's, lies in the other's patchset range; a change closed without integration is below nothing, and changes with one head exclude nothing from each other. Where a dispatch records both the session that dispatched it and the executor it bound, one `lineage` record per distinct pair is written, at the earliest such dispatch: tier `bound`, `at` the dispatch, `label` the binding's handle, and `subject` the change or journal artifact. A native child is linked by its recording and writes none. The `lineage` records come first, by time, parent and child, then each session's bindings and events, by session, time and work. Two exports of an unchanged ledger differ only in `written_at`, which also ends each span of a run still open. Evidence tapes would stop reading before its end is refused and nothing is written: standard output carries one file, of at most 10,000 records after the header, and a longer export is refused naming `--output-dir`. `--output-dir DIR` writes `evidence-0001.jsonl`, `evidence-0002.jsonl`, ... into DIR, which must be absent or an empty directory and is checked before the ledger is read, and leaves standard output empty. Name order is write order; each file is the header, with one `written_at` for every file, followed by at most 10,000 records, which keep the export's order and are never split. Evidence that would need more than the 1,000 files tapes reads from a directory, or that holds a line longer than 256 KiB, which no file holds whole, is refused either way. The files are written beside DIR and moved into place together, so a failure leaves DIR as it was. Standard error summarizes the sessions written, the records by kind, the commits that still appear under several labels, the sessions without a figure, the sessions the ledger does not divide, the runs still open, and with `--output-dir` the files written. Every session is measured as `cost show` measures it, so the read takes as long. Reads the ledger and the recordings and records no event; read the file with `tapes usage SESSION --evidence FILE`, and a directory with `tapes usage SESSION --evidence DIR`
